<title>POLAND: Polifarb Wroclaw resumes production.</title>
<headline>Polifarb Wroclaw resumes production.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish paintmaker Polifarb Wroclaw SA resumed on July 20 the sale of its products and on Tuesday also re-started production after a brief shut-down caused by flooding, the company said in a Wednesday statement.</p>
<p>&quot;After the flood wave retreated, Polifarb Wroclaw resumed on July 20 the sale of its products. (And) after neccessary repairs the company resumed on July 22 its production which will be gradually expanded,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>The company gave no further details.</p>
<p>The company has been suspended from Warsaw bourse trade since July 14 due to flooding.</p>
<p>The Warsaw Stock Exchange would resume trade in the company once it submits official statements on the scope of losses suffered during the flooding.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
